+# Current callback capture — inactive diagnostic proposal
+
+A small UI-test-side collector for the **actual** `XCUIAccessibilityAuditIssue`. No root integration, app hooks, receipts, launch-environment attestation, source-SHA gate or exemption API is included. Four native metadata tests are prepared; none has been compiled or executed here.
+
+## Capture contract
+
+`CurrentCallbackCapture.collect(issue:screenKey:callbackIndex:auditContextID:attach:)` returns a read-only `Capture`, **not** the issue handler's Bool. Its runtime entry point accepts no screenshot, path or digest. It retains `issue.element` once and performs:
+
+1. Snapshot A of that exact object.
+2. Fresh `XCUIScreen.main.screenshot().pngRepresentation` A.
+3. Fresh `XCUIScreen.main.screenshot().pngRepresentation` B.
+4. Snapshot B of the same retained object.
+
+Both tuples contain exact raw element type, stable identifier, label, unrounded frame and accessible `elementState` (`isEnabled`, `isSelected`). Missing/anonymous snapshots, any tuple change, nonfinite/invalid geometry, wrong audit kind or bad timing make the capture incomplete. These state flags are **not rendering traits**. Target font, dynamic type, SwiftUI environment and color/accessibility overrides remain explicitly `unknown-not-exposed-by-xctest`; the collector never reads UIKit traits from the test runner. `hasFocus` is deliberately omitted rather than claiming platform-independent support.
+
+Six native-local monotonic times bracket the snapshots and two PNG captures. Ordering, finite/nonnegative values and a fixed **five-second** maximum are checked. XCTest's synchronous calls cannot be cancelled by this collector; an overrun is rejected once it returns, and the enclosing native test still needs its normal finite execution timeout. Hashing and attaching occur after the final snapshot and are outside this capture interval.
+
+Each PNG is retained and attached as the **original Data bytes** (`public.png`), with its internally computed SHA-256/byte count in JSON and a companion `.sha256` attachment. There is no UIImage conversion or re-encoding. Payloads over 32 MiB are rejected and not attached. The PNG envelope check is only a resource/header guard, not decoding or pixel proof. There are no image fixtures or large binaries in this proposal.
+
+## Integration boundary, not an activated filter
+
+The existing `AccessibilityAuditUITests.run` already keeps app-frame and hierarchy queries outside the issue handler, records findings independently, and returns `true` to let its own later assertions enforce them. Preserve that behavior. The collector should be called only in an explicitly reviewed diagnostic contrast-capture path; its output must not change `reason`, `fails`, findings, retry behavior or issue-handler return value.
+
+Illustrative placement (not applied):
+
+```swift
+// Before performAccessibilityAudit: record immutable app viewport/screen/clip/overlay context
+// under auditContextID. Do not traverse that context from inside the callback.
+let captured = CurrentCallbackCapture.collect(
+    issue: issue, screenKey: screen, callbackIndex: findings.callbacks,
+    auditContextID: auditContextID, attach: { self.add($0) })
+pendingCallbackEvidence.append(captured)
+// Continue existing finding recording and enforcement unchanged.
+```
+
+After the audit completes, observe/validate post-audit viewport and screen/clip/overlay context **outside** the callback. The UUID and screen label only correlate observations; they do not verify app identity, context completeness or absence of an intermediate overlay. Unknown or changed context must remain incomplete. Do not recurse the app hierarchy in this collector, re-resolve an ID or use a query's first match. No snapshot `children`/`dictionaryRepresentation` traversal occurs, although XCTest itself controls how it obtains the target snapshot.
+
+## Pure inspection interface
+
+The separate `CurrentCallbackRasterCheck` supplies this in-memory diagnostic entry (not invoked by the audit):
+
+```text
+inspect(capture: CurrentCallbackCapture.Capture,
+        contextBeforeAudit: immutable context,
+        contextAfterAudit: immutable context,
+        catalog: reviewed current exact-raster templates) -> diagnostic inspection
+```
+
+The helper receives the actual capture object with read-only metadata and both PNG Data payloads; there is no runtime loader for imported captures. It must check metadata completeness, exact screen/identity/state/frame, context correspondence/completeness, decode/ICC-to-sRGB/orientation/scale validity, both canonical raster matches, full-glyph/backing coverage and the required minimum contrast. A SHA identifies exact captured bytes but never substitutes for decoding, glyph proof or raster comparison. No old whole-repository SHA is a runtime acceptance criterion. Catalog review is separate and pending. Unknown target rendering traits must remain visible; if those traits are a prerequisite, the inspection remains incomplete rather than substituting runner observations. All results are diagnostic; original contrast failures stay retained.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `python tools/ci/test_current_callback_capture_contract.py` for portable source contracts only. The four native tests cover exact tuple/state changes, missing/invalid identity/geometry, timestamp bounds/order and exact-byte SHA/header behavior. Native API compilation, actual callback latency and screenshot/context coupling still require reviewed CI execution.
+
+## Official API references
+
+- [Audit issue element](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuiaccessibilityauditissue/element): optional element supplied with the actual issue.
+- [XCUIElementSnapshotProviding](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuielementsnapshotproviding) and [snapshot attributes](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuielementsnapshot): capture attributes of that element, without a separate query or descendant traversal.
+- [XCUIElementAttributes](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuielementattributes): element type, identifier, label, frame, enabled and selected state; not target rendering traits.
+- [XCUIScreenshot.pngRepresentation](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuiscreenshot/pngrepresentation): original screenshot PNG Data.
+- [XCTAttachment(data:uniformTypeIdentifier:)](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xctest/xctattachment/init(data:uniformtypeidentifier:)): attach unchanged data payloads instead of re-encoding an image.
+- [ProcessInfo.systemUptime](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/processinfo/systemuptime) and [CryptoKit SHA256](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/cryptokit/sha256): native-local observation times and exact captured-byte digests.
