+# Current callback raster check — inactive diagnostic proposal
+
+## Decision and scope
+
+An exact, color-managed **current screenshot support raster** can establish a narrow sampled contrast property without proving that every production/build input matches a historical app. Different code or traits that paint the same complete target/backing pixels have the same measured visual contrast. Source revision, build configuration and available runtime observations remain provenance; they are not an eligibility gate. No installed-app receipt, production hook, source-closure inventory, environment attestation or whole-repository SHA equality is necessary for this claim.
+
+This does not prove that the correct release was distributed, all runtime states are accessible, every effective SwiftUI trait was observed, or the accessibility auditor sampled the same instant. Those are different claims. Ordinary CI provenance still identifies what was tested; malicious test-runner/artifact substitution is outside this visual test's threat model, as it is for existing XCTest assertions.
+
+**Nothing is activated.** `Measurement.auditAuthorization` is permanently false in this proposal. No audit call site, original finding, exception list, app source, workflow or acceptance criterion is changed. The existing two-case runtime helper remains untouched.
+
+## Small implementation
+
+- `CurrentCallbackCapture`: UI-test-side collection from the actual issue object; snapshot A, screen PNG A, screen PNG B, snapshot B. Captures use the same retained issue element, not ID lookup or first match. Immutable type/ID/label/unrounded frame/enabled/selected must agree; PNG bytes are retained and attached unchanged, and internally hashed. Five-second monotonic bound, no imported screenshot path. Effective target rendering traits are explicitly unknown.
+- `CurrentCallbackRasterCheck`: accepts that private-initialized in-memory capture and externally observed pre/post context under the same request UUID. Both contexts must agree on screen, actual viewport/clear bounds, exclusions and exactly one complete identity tuple. A UUID correlates evidence; it is not an observation of screen state. Any unknown/ambiguous context must prevent construction/use of a qualified context.
+- Ten compact catalog candidates, pinned by catalog/resource/raw-RGBA hashes. Reference source SHA is recorded, never compared with a current SHA. Full support is the reported AX frame plus **eight physical pixels on all sides**, not the AX frame alone. Target cores and backing masks are inherited from independently reviewed native-reference analysis and displayed for review. Whole expanded support, including antialiasing, whitespace and margin, must match exactly after color conversion: **zero channel tolerance**, no alignment, resizing, mask regeneration or percentage-of-good-pixels rule.
+- Every foreground role is measured against the worst extrema of the whole reviewed backing support, not a favorable nearest point or average. All ten original reference minima exceed 4.5; the smallest is **5.298798:1** for catalogue 03. The two LV paint roles are independently checked. No large-text threshold reduction.
+- Input PNG orientation must be up; dimensions and bit depth are bounded. Core Graphics draws from a known RGB profile into an explicit sRGB destination. Original bytes must contain one CRC-valid sRGB declaration or one bounded, valid embedded RGB ICC profile; missing/default-assigned, duplicate, malformed, late or unsupported declarations reject. The decoded color space must match that declaration before conversion. Unknown/device RGB rejects. Physical mapping derives from observed viewport and pixel dimensions; UIImage point/scale metadata never supplies geometry. Nonopaque support rejects.
+
+The old two-case `AuditContrastPixelProof` is a useful narrow capture pattern, but its component counts, ink fractions and color bands are **not exact glyph identity**. The former 13-case proposal also cropped only the AX frame and allowed a four-level raster tolerance. This proposal reuses the useful native references while replacing those weaknesses, not broadening that old policy.
+
+## Reference coverage and exclusions
+
+The ten proposed support plots include five LV instances, Win a round, Songs hero eyebrow/title, selected All and cover catalogue 03. The reference PNGs came from the same documented native run, tested merge `78060e534a69759b37cf50adac6b7f4d80ef4325`; this is reference provenance, not the current candidate SHA. The eyebrow/title use the fresh native reference rather than widening tolerance for their changed older rasters.
+
+The cover-line Jingle, Bells and Ode to templates are excluded. Their earlier color masks touched AX crop boundaries; padded original inspection shows that Jingle/Bells rectangles overlap neighboring-line ink. A reviewed combined title-block support is a possible later solution, not included here. There is no inference that an AX frame itself bounds every glyph.
+
+All **18 previously obscured/clipped/edge-faded targets**, all three currently anonymous callbacks, unrecognized E7, every other unknown identity, and any target/support intersecting a known clip/overlay remain rejected. A target inside a viewport or above a tab-bar frame alone is not proof of unobscured full glyph coverage. The separate reveal collector remains separate: it does not clear the original finding or inherit these templates.
+
+The reference-support contact sheet has been independently inspected: all ten strings appear complete with surrounding backing. That review is **not a native helper pass, a current callback pair, or authorization**. Catalog status stays inactive and unreleased pending native tests and fresh paired callbacks.
+
+## Coupling limit — explicitly unresolved by build receipts
+
+Apple documents screenshots as the UI state at the time of screenshot capture. The audit issue does not expose the auditor's sampled raster or an atomic audit-snapshot-screenshot transaction. Matching before/after issue snapshots, two identical support rasters, an isolated contrast request, resting scene and unchanged pre/post context reduce accidental misassociation; they cannot rule out every intermediate transient or establish the auditor's original sampling instant.
+
+Consequently this implementation reports only **two sampled current raster observations with bounded callback-local correlation**. It must not retrospectively erase an earlier failure or be described as an atomic proof. If the scene changes, context cannot be observed, the audit does not complete, or callback/screenshot coupling remains questionable, keep the original failure. A full build/installed-app attestation would not fix this temporal gap.
+
+The code deliberately does not read UIKit rendering traits in the UI-test runner or treat launch arguments as observed app traits. Available run configuration may be recorded as provenance. Unavailable effective traits remain unknown. Exact actual pixels, identity, known geometry and stability are still required.
+
+## Minimal integration sequence, not performed
+
+1. Review these four Swift files and the ten expanded raw/support-mask plots. Keep all original enforcement untouched. Run the portable tests below; their success is not native compilation.
+2. Include `CurrentContrastFixtures` as an explicit **folder resource** in `TimbreUITests`, excluding it from the broad source glob to avoid flattened/duplicated resources. Do the same for the disposable `CurrentContrastOriginals` folder after materialization. No resource belongs in the production app.
+3. Obtain the reference visual artifact through the existing authorized CI artifact path, verify its pinned archive hash, and materialize only the six deduplicated original PNGs with `materialize_current_contrast_originals.py`. They total about 8.27 MB and are **not committed**. Missing originals fail the native test; do not skip them or replace them with synthetic canvases.
+4. Select these standalone XCTest classes in the existing UI-test unit-test invocation: `CurrentCallbackCaptureTests`, `CurrentCallbackRasterCheckTests`, and `CurrentCallbackOriginalRasterTests`. Preserve `AuditContrastPixelProofTests` and every existing test selector. No app diagnostic compile flag is needed.
+5. For the next explicitly diagnostic isolated contrast run only, collect immutable actual pre-audit hierarchy/context outside the callback. Derive viewport, selected screen, unique complete tuple, clipping and known overlay bounds from observations; never copy catalog bounds as observations. If completeness cannot be established, keep the result incomplete. Call `CurrentCallbackCapture.collect` inside the existing handler for candidate exact contrast issues, queue captures, and continue recording/enforcing every original failure unchanged.
+6. Observe post-audit context outside the handler. Require completed audit, same context request, stable observed context and exact tuple uniqueness before calling `inspect(capture:...)`. Attach the diagnostic measurement, metadata and both original PNGs. No recursion through the whole app during the issue callback, no scrolling/reveal/retry-to-green, no assignment to `reason`, no change to `fails` or return Bool.
+7. Inspect fresh native PNG pairs and measure callback duration. Native Core Graphics/PNG orientation/profile behavior, XCTest APIs, test resource packaging and the context wiring remain unexecuted. Fresh current-state raster mismatch stays failure, even if it looks like harmless rendering drift. Any future activation requires separate explicit approval; this package contains none.
+
+The proposed context consumer/wiring is intentionally not synthesized from unobserved application state. It is a small remaining call-site task, not a reason to add a production trust subsystem.
+
+## Commands
+
+```sh
+# Disposable diagnostic environment; the repository marketing venv does not include NumPy/SciPy.
+python3 -m venv /tmp/current-contrast-venv
+/tmp/current-contrast-venv/bin/python -m pip install -r tools/ci/requirements-current-contrast.txt
+/tmp/current-contrast-venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tools/ci -p 'test_current_*.py'
+python3 tools/ci/materialize_current_contrast_originals.py \
+  --catalog ios/TimbreUITests/CurrentContrastFixtures/catalog.json \
+  --screenshots "$VERIFIED_CALLBACK_SCREENSHOTS" \
+  --output ios/TimbreUITests/CurrentContrastOriginals
+```
+
+Native resource example (merge into the existing target, do not duplicate its source glob):
+
+```yaml
+sources:
+  - path: TimbreUITests
+    excludes: [CurrentContrastFixtures, CurrentContrastOriginals]
+  - path: TimbreUITests/CurrentContrastFixtures
+    type: folder
+    buildPhase: resources
+  - path: TimbreUITests/CurrentContrastOriginals
+    type: folder
+    buildPhase: resources
+```
+
+## Official references
+
+- [W3C G18](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Techniques/general/G18): sRGB luminance, immediate backing, each letter and minimum 4.5 contrast. This is a sampled visual check, not a claim of complete WCAG conformance.
+- [XCUIScreenshot](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuiscreenshot) and [screenshot()](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuiscreenshotproviding/screenshot()): current screenshot state, not a guaranteed audit sampling instant.
+- [XCUIAccessibilityAuditIssue](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcuiautomation/xcuiaccessibilityauditissue): issue element and descriptions, without the auditor's original raster.
+- [CGColorSpace](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcolorspace), [copyICCData()](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcolorspace/copyiccdata()), [CGContext.draw](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcontext/draw(_:in:)): profile interpretation and drawing to the sRGB destination.
+- [CGImageSourceCreateWithData](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/imageio/cgimagesourcecreatewithdata(_:_:)), [CGImageSourceCopyPropertiesAtIndex](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/imageio/cgimagesourcecopypropertiesatindex(_:_:_:)) and [kCGImagePropertyOrientation](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/imageio/kcgimagepropertyorientation): decode original PNG metadata without silently rotating it.
+- [XcodeGen project sources](https://github.com/yonaskolb/XcodeGen/blob/master/Docs/ProjectSpec.md#sources): explicit folder references and build-phase selection for test-only resources.
+
+## Source PNG profile regression
+
+The decoder validates original chunk boundaries and CRCs and accepts exactly one explicit sRGB or iCCP
+source declaration before image data. Embedded ICC inflation is capped at 1 MiB via the platform zlib
+module; Core Graphics validates its RGB profile and the ImageIO-decoded color space must compare equal.
+The existing destination drawing still performs conversion to sRGB. Native coverage strips actual PNG
+profile chunks, confirms ImageIO still decodes those bytes, then requires both decodePNG and inspect
+to reject them; a real linear-sRGB ICC PNG exercises conversion rather than profile reassignment.
+This new native test and SDK zlib import remain uncompiled/unrun here. All measurements remain
+diagnostic-only with authorization false.
+
+The originals materializer uses only Python's standard library (`python3 -S ... --help` is tested).
+NumPy, Pillow and SciPy are needed only for portable raster checks/fixture construction; the optional
+diagnostic requirements file is explicit and does not change any app or repository-wide environment.
+
+References: [PNG source color declarations](https://www.w3.org/TR/png-3/#11iCCP),
+[zlib bounded uncompress and CRC interfaces](https://zlib.net/manual.html),
+[CGColorSpace.init(iccData:)](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcolorspace/init(iccdata:)).
